    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d321">

                <pb facs="0824" n="702" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg702"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr.
                            de Claparède.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1889-05-27"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 27,
                        1889</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Acknowledging the receipt of your note of
                    the 17th instant, concerning the action of the authorities of this country in
                    sending certain Swiss immigrants back to Europe, I have the honor to inform you
                    that inquiries have been made in the proper quarters in relation to the matter
                    and that the replies will be duly communicated to your legation when
                    received.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James G. Blaine.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
